# Nightdesk keys
#
# Copy this file to .env in the repository root, then fill in the keys you have:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Leave the rest blank or delete the lines. A blank line means "not set".
# Run `nightdesk doctor` at any time to see which sources are ready.
# .env is git-ignored: never commit it.
#
# The Belgian Infrabel punctuality file is public and needs no key, so you can
# start with an empty .env.

# --- Netherlands: NS engineering works -------------------------------------
# Free key from the NS developer portal. Feeds `nightdesk fetch-ns`.
NS_API_KEY=

# --- Germany: DB station boards --------------------------------------------
# Free key pair from the DB API Marketplace. Subscribe to the "OpenBoards"
# product (the older Timetables product is being retired; new subscriptions
# are no longer accepted). Both values are needed.
# Feeds `nightdesk fetch-db-timetables`.
DB_CLIENT_ID=
DB_API_KEY=

# --- Switzerland: SIRI planned disruptions ---------------------------------
# Free token from opentransportdata.swiss. Feeds `nightdesk fetch-swiss-siri`.
SWISS_OTD_TOKEN=

# --- Train Archive: daily trips by train number ----------------------------
# Feeds `nightdesk fetch-train-archive`.
TRAIN_ARCHIVE_TOKEN=

# --- Mistral: optional drafting of work fields from a notice ---------------
# Only used by `nightdesk text` and only when a case folder has recorded consent.
# Everything else works without it.
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
